{"xson":[{"/iati-activities/iati-activity":[{"/activity-date":[{"@iso-date":"2012-09-21","@type":"2"},{"@iso-date":"2018-12-31","@type":"4"}],"/activity-status@code":"4","/collaboration-type@code":"2","/contact-info":[{"/organisation/narrative":[{"1":"International Fund for Agricultural Development","@xml:lang":"EN"}],"/person-name/narrative":[{"1":"Achancho, Valantine Mr","@xml:lang":"EN"}],"/telephone":[{"1":"+390654591"}],"/website":[{"1":"http://www.ifad.org"}],"@type":"1"}],"/default-aid-type":[{"@code":"C01","@vocabulary":"1"}],"/default-tied-status@code":"5","/description":[{"/narrative":[{"1":"Project development objectiveThe overall goal is to improve the food security of rural people in the Maradi,Tahoua and Zinder regions. The development objective is to raise the incomes of65,000 rural households in 30 communes the Maradi, Tahoua and Zinder regions.The impact indicators are as follows: (i) 80 per cent of target households enjoygreater food security, and therefore experience a shorter lean season; (ii) 70 percent of target households increase their incomes by 50 per cent;(iii) 65,000 households benefit from services under the project; and(iv) 70 per cent of people receive training (for literacy) and are able to read andwrite.The outcomes of the two technical components are expected to contribute to theachievement of the development objective: (i) a sustainable increase in theproductivity of irrigated areas, and strengthened local capacity to manage waterresources and (ii) better transportation and marketing of products generated bysmall-scale irrigation.","@xml:lang":"EN"}]}],"/document-link":[{"/category":[{"@code":"A02"},{"@code":"A07"},{"@code":"A08"}],"/language":[{"@code":"EN"}],"/title/narrative":[{"1":"Brazil 1100001619: Paulo Freire Project Supervision Report November 2021","@xml:lang":"EN"}],"@format":"APPLICATION/PDF","@url":"https://operations.ifad.org/documents/654016/53b4257c-8b70-4e58-8adb-fca7aa62fc6c"},{"/category":[{"@code":"A07"},{"@code